|~ `::each`, the kind of a map in a shape whose values share one shape,
   and the laws declared under it.
   The decisions it exists for: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:each
  |~~ An each stands in the shape of a value for a map whose values all
      have one shape, the map a reader's data keys by ids, dates or
      names, over its first key and that shape, the one key standing for
      all of them: `{:"17" {:id 1} :"42" {:id 2}} | shape` answers
      `::shape::each{:"17" {:id ::number}}`. The key shown tells how the
      keys of the data read, and a path of the data through it reads the
      shape, `/17/id` answering `::number`; `keys` reads the rest. A map
      folds so where its keys are data, a key that reads as no name, a
      date, an id of digits, an address, over values of any kind, atoms
      among them, and where its names are many, more than eight, over
      maps, vectors, sets, values under a tag or null. A map of fewer
      names keeps them, the fields a reader reads by `get`, as a map of
      names over atoms does, `{:x 1 :y 2} | shape` answering
      `::shape{:x ::number :y ::number}`, and a map whose values part
      keeps its keys as well. Records merge in a fold as they merge in a
      vector, and a null among the values marks the fold `::nullable`; a
      vector of such maps is `[::each{…}]`, a map of vectors `::each[…]`.
      ::link~(::shape | doc) ::link~(::any/shape | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | proves :foldsAMapKeyedByData
        |~~ A map keyed by data folds over its first key. ~~|
        ~({:"17" {:id 1} :"42" {:id 2}} | shape | eq ::shape::each{:"17" {:id ::number}})
    | proves :foldsAtomsKeyedByData
        |~~ A map keyed by data folds over atoms as well. ~~|
        ~({:"2024-01-01" 3 :"2024-01-02" 5} | shape | eq ::shape::each{:"2024-01-01" ::number})
    | proves :readsThePathThroughTheKeyItShows
        |~~ A path of the data through the key shown reads the shape. ~~|
        ~({:"17" {:id 1} :"42" {:id 2}} | shape | get /17/id | eq ::number)
    | proves :keepsAFewNamesAsARecord
        |~~ A map of a few names keeps them, the fields `get` reads. ~~|
        ~({:db {:host "h"} :cache {:host "c"}} | shape | eq ::shape{:db {:host ::string} :cache {:host ::string}})
    | proves :foldsManyNamesOfOneShape
        |~~ A map of more than eight names of one shape folds. ~~|
        ~({:a {:n 1} :b {:n 2} :c {:n 3} :d {:n 4} :e {:n 5} :f {:n 6} :g {:n 7} :h {:n 8} :i {:n 9}} | shape | eq ::shape::each{:a {:n ::number}})
    | proves :keepsTheFieldsOfAMapOfAtoms
        |~~ A map of names over atoms keeps its keys. ~~|
        ~({:x 1 :y 2} | shape | eq ::shape{:x ::number :y ::number})
    | proves :keepsTheKeysOfValuesOfOtherKinds
        |~~ A map whose values part keeps its keys. ~~|
        ~({:"1" {:id 1} :"2" [1]} | shape | eq ::shape{:"1" {:id ::number} :"2" [::number]})
    | proves :keepsTheKeyOfAMapOfOne
        |~~ A map of one name keeps it. ~~|
        ~({:users [1]} | shape | eq ::shape{:users [::number]})
